6 review on CRC-derived EVs and gut microbiota. EV-focused mechanism. Good for Ch3 (mechanisms - EVs), Ch2 (CRC).\n\nP0558: 2025 abstract on ICI administration timing and survival. Circadian timing, not microbiome-specific. Limited direct relevance. Could be Ch4 (context - timing factors) with caveats.\n\nP0559: 2024 review on microbial metabolites as regulators of anti-tumor immunity. Metabolite-focused. Good for Ch3 (mechanisms - metabolites).\n\nP0560: 2022 review on gut microbiota and tumor immune escape. Comprehensive. Good for Ch2, Ch3, Ch4, Ch5.\n\nP0561: 2021 review on tumor neoantigen mimicry by microbial species. Specific mechanism (molecular mimicry). Good for Ch3 (mechanisms).\n\nP0562: 2025 abstract on ICI in RCC. RCC-specific, mentions microbiome modulation as emerging strategy. Limited microbiome detail. Could be Ch2, Ch4 with caveats.\n\nP0563: 2025 review on gut microbiota metabolites and TME communication. Metabolite-focused. Good for Ch3 (mechanisms), Ch2.\n\nP0564: 2021 review on microbiome and antibiotics influence on ICI efficacy. Good for Ch2, Ch4 (antibiotics).\n\nP0565: 2026 systematic review on gut microbiome and ICI response in melanoma. Melanoma-specific. Good for Ch2, Ch6 (heterogeneity/methodology).\n\nP0566: 2026 review on microbiome as prediction of immunotherapy response in lung cancer. NSCLC-focused. Good for Ch2, Ch4, Ch6.\n\nP0567: 2024 review on harnessing gut microbiome for cancer immunotherapy. Comprehensive. Good for Ch2, Ch3, Ch5, Ch6.\n\nP0568: 2025 review on ICI mechanism and advances with microbiome section. Good for Ch2, Ch3, Ch4.\n\nP0569: 2024 abstract on longitudinal gut microbiome assessment in NSCLC neoadjuvant immunotherapy. NSCLC-specific, neoadjuvant setting. Good for Ch2, Ch4 (treatment context).\n\nP0570: 2024 paper on tumor-associated carbohydrates as link between microbiome and ICI. Specific mechanism hypothesis (carbohydrate/antibody-mediated). Good for Ch3 (mechanisms).\n\nP0571: 2025 review on gut microbiome and circadian rhythms. General microbiome-circadian interaction, not ICI-specific. Limited direct relevance. Could be Ch4 (context - circadian factors) with caveats.\n\nP0572: 2021 review on therapeutic interventions and mechanisms of gut microbiota-mediated ICI modulation. Good for Ch3, Ch5, Ch6.\n\nP0573: 2025 review on optimizing FMT for ICI efficacy. FMT-focused. Good for Ch5 (interventions), Ch3 (mechanisms).\n\nP0574: 2026 review on gut dysbiosis in oncology as risk factor for immunoresistance. Comprehensive. Good for Ch2, Ch3, Ch4, Ch5, Ch6.\n\nP0575: 2026 study on antibiotic timing and survival after ICI initiation. Large retrospective cohort. Good for Ch4 (antibiotic timing), Ch2 (clinical evidence).\n\nP0576: 2026 review on antibiotic therapy impact on immunotherapy effectiveness. Antibiotic-focused. Good for Ch4, Ch2.\n\nP0577: 2025 MIMic phase 1 trial on FMT + anti-PD1 in melanoma. Clinical trial data. Good for Ch5 (interventions), Ch2 (clinical evidence).\n\nP0578: 2026 MITRIC phase 2a trial on FMT in solid cancers resistant to ICI. Negative results. Good for Ch5 (interventions - limitations), Ch6 (challenges).\n\nP0579: 2025 study on ccRCC mouse model of ICI resistance. Not microbiome-focused, tumor microenvironment-focused. Limited direct relevance to microbiome question. Could",
